questions.stem:
Using the bond enthalpy data below, calculate $\Delta H$ for the reaction:
$$2\text{H}_2(g) + \text{O}_2(g) \rightarrow 2\text{H}_2\text{O}(g)$$
\begin{align*}
E(\text{H--H}) &= 436\ \text{kJ mol}^{-1}\\
E(\text{O=O}) &= 498\ \text{kJ mol}^{-1}\\
E(\text{O--H}) &= 463\ \text{kJ mol}^{-1}
\end{align*}

questions.solution:
Let $\theta=\tan^{-1}2+\tan^{-1}3$. Then
$$\tan\theta=\frac{2+3}{1-(2)(3)}=-1.$$
Since both angles are in quadrant I, $\theta$ lies in quadrant II; hence $\cos\theta=-\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{1+\tan^2\theta}}=-\dfrac{1}{\sqrt2}$.}
